## Classes

| Class | What it covers | The row records |
|---|---|---|
| `D` our decision | The bid team's call: commercial levers, SLAs, process timings, contract positions, wording, named people already proposed in project files, delivery locations from known offices | The decision (Value) and its basis |
| `R` public fact | Anything a public source settles — closed by `eng-bid-research` | The question (Basis) and the interim wording (Value) |
| `X` firm-only input | Client consent to name a client; whether a certificate or letter is actually held; internal headcounts; registrations; individual availability | The client-facing fallback wording (Value) that stands if the input never arrives, and what the firm must confirm (Basis) |

**Status:** `decided` — our call, not yet approved · `pending` — sent for approval · `approved` ·
`rejected` — the approver said no; Value must change · `changed` — Value edited, not yet synced ·
`confirmed` — an X input arrived and the Value is now fact.

**Columns.** `Value` is the exact string the response states. `Applied value` is the string
currently in the listed sections — leave it empty; `/eng-sync` fills it on the first sync and
rewrites `Applied value` → `Value` in the sections whenever the two differ. `Sections` = comma-
separated section file names; `Slides` = optional slide numbers.

